avionmesh-pi: isolated Raspberry Pi / Linux bridge development project, 2026-11-06.
Distributed under LGPL-3.0-only; see LICENSE and accompanying COPYING.GPLv3.

Protocol logic is adapted into Python from oyvindkinsey/recsrmesh-cpp
(MCP receive crypto, header layout, MTL constants), oyvindkinsey/avionmesh-cpp
(command encoding), and local extensions to oyvindkinsey/esphome-avionmesh
(controller event decoding). Original projects are LGPL-3.0. Copyright in the
original contributions remains with their respective authors and contributors.
The checked source files contain no additional author copyright notice.

Inspected reference hashes and repository revisions are recorded in
docs/PROVENANCE.json; private deployment records remain outside this snapshot. Local changes are not represented as upstream releases.
Python receive pipeline, validation, replay CLI, fixtures, container setup and
tests are new work. No browser assets, private inventories or captures copied.
Cryptography is provided by the separately installed cryptography package;
its own notices and licenses remain in its installed distribution.

Version 0.2 adds a Python MASP/ECDH port from the local recsrmesh ACK-validation
reference and guarded table-editor behavior from the staged ESP source 586ebb8.
The recsrmesh-cpp maintainer's licensing commit 726c2b28420eb336366a2ec1036efc1dd2a6bc60
(2026-10-18) explicitly declares LGPL-3.0-or-later and adds the LGPLv3 LICENSE.
Its older README's GPL label is treated as stale based on that commit and file.
The publication license review records the evidence. Upstream license grants,
including later-version options, are retained; this project's existing
LGPL-3.0-only declaration is unchanged. GitHub publication is separate from
hardware qualification.

Version 0.3 also derives lifecycle, keypad onboarding/checkpoint recovery,
Accessory enrollment, scoped dimmer assignment, identity hints and cloud metadata
handling from the reviewed staged ESP source archive 586ebb8. See
docs/PROVENANCE.json and the retained private development provenance.
The platform adapters and synthetic tests remain separate from operational state.

Version 0.4 capture semantics reference staged mesh_capture.h; sequence safety review references public recsrmesh csrmesh.cpp/mcp_crypto.cpp. Original notices and exact hashes are retained in docs/PROVENANCE.json.

Version 0.4.4 adds an original, narrow aiomqtt socket-lifetime adapter after
inspecting aiomqtt 2.5.1 client.py. It uses private callback/future hooks and
requires that pinned version. aiomqtt is separately installed under its BSD
license; its full notices remain in the installed distribution. No global event
loop errors are suppressed. Source reference/hash are recorded in provenance.

